      "side": 1,
      "message": "actions/checkout@v4 and actions/setup-node@v4 are pinned to a mutable tag, while socketdev/action is (correctly) pinned to a full commit SHA. Inconsistent pinning policy inside a security-oriented workflow.\n\nWhy: A supply-chain-verification workflow that itself depends on unverified upstream tags is a small but real credibility gap. If the goal is to defend against transitive package tampering, third-party GitHub Action tampering is on the same threat model. This is exactly what OpenSSF Scorecard\u0027s Pinned-Dependencies check flags.\nRecommendation: Pin actions/checkout and actions/setup-node to full commit SHAs (with the version as a trailing comment), matching the socketdev/action style:\n```\n- uses: actions/checkout@\u003c40-char-sha\u003e   # v4.x.y\n- uses: actions/setup-node@\u003c40-char-sha\u003e # v4.x.y\n```",
